# Every text file is LF on every checkout, including a checkout on Windows.
# Git for Windows writes CRLF by default. See dbmeta D89 and D110.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A test file is a copy of a real file, byte for byte. Git must not change
# it. A document format can hold CRLF line ends or binary data on purpose.
testdata/** -text
*/testdata/** -text
internal/*/testdata/** -text
